 forbid some sort of  nuclear war well then is what is to stop  president putin going on to attack other  countries just using the same nuclear  threat even countries that are members  of nato  well i i the the what is to stop him is  that this is turning into a much much  more perilous uh misadventure for putin  than i think he realized and as your  report made clear it has had a  demoralizing effect on russian forces  some of those young conscripts and it  has had uh  the effect of stealing the will of the  ukrainian people and that is how we will  ensure putin fails in ukraine and uh we  are there for the long haul and that's  why i mean again uh with some of these  very brutal tactics that we're seeing  being reported including by sky news  with the harrowing pictures that we will  see in our uh tv screens and in the  newspapers i think we've been very clear  that um those that engage in war crimes  will be held to account and the icc  prosecutors exactly that's that's  absolutely it there are war crimes  happening right now in this country  children are dying schools are being  attacked a kindergarten has been  attacked and the west is sanctioning  russian banks and kicking russia out of  the world cup  yes and but no more than that actually i  mean i i totally accept what you're  saying  this is the uh barbarous consequences of  such an appalling aggressive action by  president putin which you're not wishing  to stop which you're not stopping  so forgive me you're interrupting me at  every step and you're you're frankly uh  following this on the 24-hour news cycle  which i understand is your liberty to do  what we've said we're going to do is  degrade putin's war machine by starving  it of the finance necessary to operate  and actually if you look at the  short-term consequences the effects on  the ruble effect on the stock market the  doubling of interest rates in russia it  is having the effect that we want and it  is turning into a very very difficult  campaign for putin one which and we've  always said this will be disastrous for  russian uh for putin and for the russian  people but i do think we'll need to have  the stamina to be in this for the long  haul uh and that's why making it clear  both to putin but also to commanders in  moscow on the ground in ukraine  that they will be held accountable uh  for any violations of the laws of war  and we've shown the west has shown that  we're willing uh to to to see this  through we will not just look the other  way we had radovan karadich the butcher  the balkans end up in a british jail  cell via the hague recently  and that message will go uh to those  commanders on the ground in moscow as  well as back to uh  in ukraine as well as back to moscow and  there will be accountability uh for the  for any crimes that are committed on  ukrainian soil  and for vladimir putin accountability  for vladimir putin um when it comes to  war crimes  well  that is there as well uh he is  ultimately the person in charge uh via  command responsibility and so that is  very much a factor and this ought to  play into his calculations along with  the fact that uh as you as your reporter  uh uh quite rightly said and your your  clip were quite rightly said this has  not been the walk in the park that he  expected uh either in terms of uh  ukrainian resistance uh or the  effectiveness of his own tactics so all  of these things will slow down and we  hope uh encourage change the calculus  and get him to step back uh and  again we take these actions and the uk  has done a huge amount it's been in the  vanguard the prime minister the defense  secretary the foreign secretary  but we do this with our partners and we  are willing to to be in this for the  long haul because i suspect  notwithstanding the initial stuttering  putin will respond uh  and try seek to respond in ever more  heavy-handed ways with the appalling  humanitarian consequences that we'll  have  so what about the idea of enforcing s